## Eight bounded author lenses

- SOLID: ScopeUnionCoordinator measures a scope; actual LaneDeliveryCoordinator retains PR opening/check observation responsibilities. No delivery/merge/state capability is added.
- DRY: one existing topology priority/age policy, one existing scope-plan reader, one existing union tick/composition. Dispatch eligibility is no longer mistaken for composition membership.
- Hexagonal: tracker/Git/check-runner ports remain the only collaborators. Native facts flow through existing readers; no forge or composition-root dependency enters.
- KISS: one private typed roster helper and one readback guard; no generic orchestration framework or guessed hold/stop rule.
- Typed agent calls: no agent SDK, prompt output, model classifier or structured call contract changes. Union checks remain subprocess check-chain observations with the shipped root/cascade classifier.
- Official framework practices: existing frozen Pydantic domain carriers and existing async ownership/cleanup APIs retained; no new library patterns or settings semantics.
- Type safety: structurally neutral strict source; semantically clearer `tuple[UnionLaneBranch, ...]` replaces misuse of ScopeReadySet. Typed error contracts remain. The separately recorded optional/cross-validated UnionCompositionResult shape concern is untouched, not claimed resolved.
- Hygiene: exact isolated donor base, four-file committed slice, unchanged writer during every test run, saved failing controls, finite old-PR behavioral harvest and exact map. No PR/initiative/Notion/state writes or other worker-tree changes.

## Remaining ownership and integration

Root reviews the exact frozen commit, then integrates into the actual M5 owning branch once its shared plan/read and union prerequisites are present. Update future call sites to the actual ScopeUnionCoordinator name; do not retain the obsolete DeliveryCoordinator alias. Preserve M3's exclusive source and actual milestone ancestry. This donor-based correction is not itself a maintained M5 PR or whole M5 extraction.

F02's retained-roster mechanism and its return readback are implemented locally; production scope-walker selection and terminal/grader consumption remain explicit integration obligations under KOD587/593. KOD78's residual outcome/stopping-rule conjunction remains open ([recorded fork](https://linear.app/duckburg/issue/KOD-78#comment-ec66b3b8-29d3-4083-bd64-f5afa55738c4)); no synthetic bound or new stopping authority was invented. No change to KOD777, lane delivery's existing review guards, or union optional-result-shape review. Do not close PR114 until root independently reviews this accepted behavior replacement plus disposition of its rejected scanners; no other old PR closure follows from this slice.
